---
pagination:
  # Convoy has a real page (src/tajima-convoy.njk), so it is excluded in
  # _data/locationStubs.js. Do NOT filter with `pagination.before` here:
  # `before` must be a real function, YAML cannot express one, and a string is
  # ignored silently rather than erroring.
  data: locationStubs
  size: 1
  alias: loc
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "{{ loc.url }}"
pageKey: locationStub
eleventyComputed:
  title: "Tajima Ramen {{ loc.name }} | {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }}"
  description: "Tajima Ramen {{ loc.name }}, {{ loc.address.street }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}. Address and phone. Walk in, no reservations."
---
{#
  ============================ STUB PAGES ============================

  Built originally for one reason: /locations/ is a P1 page that linked to
  six URLs that did not exist. Six 404s off the site's router is worse than
  six thin pages behind a noindex. All five paginate over this one template;
  which five carry noindex today is no longer uniform, see below.

  CONTENT RULE FOR THIS TEMPLATE: everything on the page comes from
  locations.json, which carries the SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md NAP table. Nothing is
  written here. The one line of prose per location is the `summary` field,
  which was already sourced from CLIENT_FACTS.md for the /locations/ cards, not
  drafted tonight.

  STATUS AS OF 2026-09-17, from the mobile audit's stub readiness report.
  `noindex` is computed per room in location-stub.11tydata.js, not a blanket
  true here any more:

    READY, noindex dropped: Crown Point, Mercury, East Village. Each has a
    differentiator section, a full menu from its own Toast catalog, confirmed
    hours, and a full FAQ, the same standard the two hand-written pages meet.

    STILL NOINDEXED: Plaza Bonita, blocked on room photography nobody has
    shot yet. Maui, blocked on hours nobody has supplied and a differentiator
    section deliberately deferred to a client decision (see the `_maui` note
    in roomDifferences.json).

  Hours: confirmed for four of five (locations.json `_hoursNote`, 2026-09-09).
  Only Maui lacks a real hours array; it has a `closesAt` field instead,
  which is a closing time, not a weekly pattern, and is not enough for
  openingHoursSpecification.

  Menu, sameAs (GBP/Yelp) and a plate.njk happy-hour row (for rooms with a bar
  program) are live for all five: none of these is an outstanding gap. What
  is still missing from every stub, not a per-room gap: the nearest-neighbour
  link the two hand-written pages carry inconsistently between themselves
  (Convoy links Mercury; College Heights links nothing).

  PHOTOGRAPHY. The hero and gallery below render only for a location with a
  curated entry in _data/roomPhotos.js. All seven rooms currently carry
  Connor's 2026-09-09 supplied set, machine-processed and flagged aiUpscaled
  in photos.json: this branch exists so Sam can review it in place, restored
  here 2026-09-17 after briefly coming out. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md's rule (Sam
  confirms the rooms, or the AI-enhanced set comes out) governs what merges to
  main, not what a noindexed preview branch shows the person doing the
  reviewing. Mercury and East Village additionally have real, non-preview
  photography of their own food (see `dishes` in roomPhotos.js), unaffected
  either way. See the PREVIEW BRANCH ONLY note at the top of roomPhotos.js for
  the full picture, including which rooms have genuine photography to fall
  back on once this set is confirmed or dropped.
#}
{%- set gallery = roomPhotos[loc.id] %}

{%- set spriteIcons = ["chopsticks-noodles", "naruto", "ramen-bowl"] %}
{#- Plus whatever marks menuConcepts gives the module's sections, so a new
    section cannot ship a <use> pointing at a symbol this page never emitted. -#}
{%- set spriteIcons = spriteIcons | withMenuIcons(menuConcepts) %}
{% include "components/icon-sprite.njk" %}
{% include "components/menu-marks.njk" %}

{#- PREVIEW BRANCH: the stub hero gains a photo slot when the location has a
    curated hero. Gated, so Maui (which has none) renders the original
    single-column hero rather than an empty frame. -#}
<section class="page-hero{% if gallery.hero %} page-hero--split{% endif %}" aria-labelledby="page-title">
  <div class="page-hero__inner">
   <div>
    <p class="page-hero__crumbs">
      <a href="/">{{ site.name }}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/locations/">Locations</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="page-hero__crumbs-current">{{ loc.name }}</span>
    </p>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title" id="page-title">{{ loc.name }}</h1>
    <p class="page-hero__lede">{{ loc.summary }}</p>

    {% include "components/plate.njk" %}
   </div>

    {%- if gallery.hero %}
    <figure class="page-hero__photo">
      <img class="page-hero__photo-img"
        src="{{ gallery.hero.src }}"
        alt="{{ gallery.hero.alt }}"
        loading="lazy" width="{{ gallery.hero.width }}" height="{{ gallery.hero.height }}">
      <figcaption class="page-hero__photo-cap">{{ gallery.hero.caption }}</figcaption>
    </figure>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

{% include "components/location-jump.njk" %}

{% include "components/location-place.njk" %}

{# ==================== WHAT'S DIFFERENT HERE ====================
   The section SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md calls "the one section that must not be
   templated". Cells come from _data/roomDifferences.json, where each room's
   set is hand written from CLIENT_FACTS.md for that room and nothing is
   generated. The loop renders them; it does not author them.

   Four of the five stubs have a set. Maui has none on purpose: see the _maui
   note in that file. A room with no set simply renders no section, which is
   the same graceful-degradation rule the galleries follow.

   This was the biggest structural gap between the stubs and the two full
   location pages, and it is the main reason Plaza Bonita and Maui read as
   near-duplicates of each other. #}
{%- set diffCells = roomDifferences[loc.id] %}
{%- if diffCells %}
<section class="sect pattern-section" aria-labelledby="diff-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="diff-title">What is different about <em>this room.</em></h2>
    </header>

    <div class="diff">
      {%- for cell in diffCells %}
      <article class="cell diff__cell{% if loop.first %} diff__cell--wide{% endif %} reveal">
        <h3 class="diff__title">{{ cell.title }}</h3>
        <p class="diff__body">{{ cell.body }}</p>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#
  The room, where we have it. Same component /tajima-college-heights/ uses, so
  a stub that graduates keeps the section it already had.
#}
{%- if gallery.gallery %}
  {%- set gallerySet = gallery.gallery %}
  {%- set galleryId = "room-title" %}
  {%- set galleryTitle = "The room, <em>photographed.</em>" %}
  {%- set galleryIcon = false %}
  {%- set galleryNote = false %}
  {% include "components/location-gallery.njk" %}
{%- endif %}

{#
  This kitchen's own food, added 2026-08-05. Separate set from the room
  photography and separately gated, because Mercury and East Village have food
  frames but no usable room frames, and the reverse is true at Crown Point.
  Renders nothing for a location with neither.
#}
{%- if gallery.dishes %}
  {%- set gallerySet = gallery.dishes %}
  {%- set galleryId = "dishes-title" %}
  {#- Retitled 2026-09-09. This said "What comes out of this room", which is
      now the heading of the menu section below it, and the bowl icon moved
      there with it: one mark per page, on the section that carries the list
      rather than the photographs of it. -#}
  {%- set galleryTitle = "From this kitchen, <em>photographed.</em>" %}
  {%- set galleryIcon = false %}
  {%- set galleryNote = 'Shot at this location, not borrowed from another room.' %}
  {% include "components/location-gallery.njk" %}
{%- endif %}

{# ==================== WHAT THIS ROOM SERVES ====================
   Section 4 of the location page template, which these five pages did not
   have at all. Rows come from menu.json filtered by this room's `locations`,
   derived from the live Toast catalogs, so Plaza Bonita shows the seven
   dishes it actually carries and not the eleven the standalone rooms do.
   See components/location-menu.njk for why there are no prices here. #}
{%- set menuLoc = loc.id %}
{% include "components/location-menu.njk" %}

{#
  ==================== HAPPY HOUR, EAST VILLAGE ONLY ====================
  Added 2026-08-05, and deliberately scoped to one room.

  East Village is the only location with a happy hour fact confirmed in
  CLIENT_FACTS.md: "Padres game-night beer specials and extended hours on home
  game nights." That is this room and no other, and it must not be widened.

  The other five rooms are NOT given this block on purpose: there is nothing
  confirmed to put in one, and a section that only says "being confirmed"
  earns nothing. When real windows arrive for a room, it gets this block.

  CORRECTED 2026-09-09. This used to justify the omission by saying the other
  rooms "already carry a Happy Hour / See times row in the address plate".
  They do not. Only the two full location templates carry that row; the stub
  plate never has. The reasoning above stands without it.

  No price. SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md's East Village brief carries "$3.50" but
  happyHour.json pulled that figure as unverified, so the two sources disagree
  and the number stays off.

  No times. Extended hours on game nights is confirmed; how extended is not.
#}
{%- if loc.id == "east-village" %}
<section class="sect sect--rule" aria-labelledby="hh-title">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <header class="sect__head">
      <h2 class="sect__title" id="hh-title">Game nights at <em>Petco.</em></h2>
      <p class="sect__note">
        This room runs beer specials on Padres home game nights, and stays open later than usual when the game is at home. The window on other days is being confirmed, so call the room and they will tell you what is running. Full picture on <a class="sect__link" href="/happy-hour/">the happy hour page</a>.
      </p>
    </header>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}

{#
  THE "STILL TO COME" SECTION IS GONE, 2026-09-16.

  It was a section about what the page did not have: "the rest of this room,
  its photographs and what is different about it, is being written". That is
  project status, and a reader who came for a phone number and a menu is not
  the audience for it. It shipped on five of seven location pages and the
  structural sweep flagged it on every one.

  Most of what it apologised for has since arrived. These pages carry the
  room's full menu from its own Toast catalog, its dietary marks, its
  photography where photography exists, and its order link. What is still
  missing is missing quietly now, which is the normal state of a page rather
  than something to announce.

  Nothing was lost with it. Its two links, this room's menu and the other
  rooms, both survive several times over on the page: /locations/ five times,
  #menu twice.

  THESE PAGES ARE STILL noindex, and that is unchanged and deliberate. See
  the header of this file. Removing the noindex is a separate decision per
  room, made after the page is written rather than as part of writing it.
#}
{% include "components/location-faq.njk" %}

{% include "components/location-order.njk" %}
